# Video Games in Humanities Education: A Case for PlayStation&apos;s &quot;Doki Doki Universe&quot;™

**Authors:** Simon-Jones, L., Jankoski, J. A.

## Abstract
The effectiveness of embedding commercial video games into higher education humanities classrooms for the purpose of improving undergraduate students' analytical skills was examined through a single game case study. This collaborative study utilized the PlayStation game &quot;Doki Doki Universe&quot;™ to address methods of game implementation, logistic use, and achievement of student learning outcomes. Student journal entries were assessed using qualitative analysis techniques. Examples of student journal entries are provided.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ1361346

